  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Consists of one accordion-folded item containing three "library" books in book pockets. The first book has title : The Mirror Business; the second has title : The local desk, and the third : Fish cake. All three pockets are stamped, respectively, Mar. 15 1996, Jul. 15 1996, Nov. 15 1996.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Three (3) section pamphlet stich binding of handmade paper and other paper. Inner books are 2 hole pamphlet stich binding.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The Mirror Business: Constructed of Salago &amp; Banana bark paper with Onyx &amp; Bank Gothic letterpress and linocuts/woodcuts. Savannah College of Art and Design owns edition number 32/50. Signed by the book artist.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The Local Desk: Constructed of handmade paper of abaca and drier lint, blended in a cuisinart, dried on windows, then ironed flat. Handset caslon 471 or broadway type setting. Contains rubber stamping. Savannah College of Art and Design owns edition number 32/50. Signed by the book artist.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Fish Cake: Constructed on handmade paper. Caslon 471 &amp; 2 letterpress Type setting with linocuts and rubberstamps from Bizarro &amp; elsewhere. Savannah College of Art and Design owns edition number 32/50. Signed by the book artist.</subfield>
  </datafield>
